  "schemaVersion": "0.2.0",
  "kind": "graph",
  "generatedAt": "2026-10-10T02:42:41.534Z",
  "title": "Reviewers always run in the container's wall",
  "summary": "The factory container is now the only place a reviewer runs. osf no longer probes for the container marker, no longer carries a per-agent sandbox check, and no longer falls back to codex's own `--sandbox read-only` mode: codex always runs with `--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`, and the container is the wall. In exchange, the review workflow keeps each reviewer's home for diagnosis: `OSF_KEEP_REVIEW_HOME=1` and `TMPDIR=/out/reviewer-home` are passed into the container, the home is uploaded as a `review-home-*` artifact, and any seeded login is deleted from the kept home before it is uploaded.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
